# OBELISK WEB PORTAL (.cursorrules / Self-Instructions)

RULE 0 (MANDATORY FIRST STEP IN EVERY SESSION / TASK):
Always visit `/botworkspace/` and specifically `/botworkspace/catalog/` FIRST before making any changes:
  - `/botworkspace/catalog/index.html`
  - `/botworkspace/catalog/rules/index.html`
  - `/botworkspace/catalog/user_directives.html`
  - `/botworkspace/catalog/repos/set_theory_prover/index.html`
  - `/botworkspace/catalog/repos/web/obelisk_web.html`
Consulting `/botworkspace/catalog/` first helps you work faster and remember more.

OPERATIONAL RULES:
1. Never hand-edit files in `generated/`. All files in `generated/` must be generated by `/ramdisk/set_theory_prover/program/html_generator.ML` and `/ramdisk/set_theory_prover/program/nbg_html_generator.ML`.
2. Every symbol, variable, constant, parenthesis, quotation/antiquotation bracket (`⟨`, `⟩`, `⟦`, `⟧`, `⦃`, `⦄`, `⟪`, `⟫`), encoding/decoding (`Enc`, `Dec`, `ᶜᵒᵈᵉ`), embedding (`Emb`, `↪`), and interpretation (`μ_A`, `eval`) must be clickable and link to its accurate canonical entry and personal symbol page (`generated/symbols/*.html`), never to an unrelated entry.
3. Never use `∈Class` in HTML or ML; `Class` is the default type (`:Class`), while `∈` is strictly object-level membership between classes. Any class comprehension `{x | φ(x)}` MUST use `Class` variables (`{(x:Class) | φ(x)}`).
4. Commit generated files to `obeliskproofassistant.github.io` and sync via `/botworkspace/scripts/ramdisk_workspace.sh sync --quiet`.
